bc.. > The only required property is that objects which compare equal have the same
hash value

This raises an issue worth noting, by the way: ideally, Rational(1,2) should hash to
the same value as 0.5. So the right hash algorithm for rational numbers would
probably be something like

try:
    return hash(float(p)/q)
except OverflowError:
  bc = min(bitcount(p), bitcount(q)) - 50
  try:
    # p and q are large but p/q has acceptable magnitude
    return float(p>>bc)/(q>>bc)
  except OverflowError:
    # give up
    return hash((p, q))

(I didn't test the above code so it might be wrong, but the principle should be clear.)

