bc.. In that case Interval must be derived from Number. 

Actually, considering Interval as a number with error bounds
then I don't feel that this contradicts with the mathematical
notions of numbers: a mathematical number is an instance of Real class.

So, the following class tree should work:

class Number(..):
class Interval(Number,..):
class Real(Number):
class Float(Real,..):
class Rational(Real):
class Fraction(Rational,..):
class Integer(Rational,..):

